From: MacRunner <noreply@macrunner.app>
Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: guard CLIENT_SURFACE_PRESENTED handler on arm64

Symptom (linker):
    Undefined symbols for architecture arm64:
      "_macdrv_client_surface_presented", referenced from:
          _macdrv_handle_event in event.o
    ld: symbol(s) not found for architecture arm64

Root cause:
    `macdrv_client_surface_presented` is defined in d3dmetal.c, which is
    wrapped in `#if defined(__x86_64__)` because D3DMetal is x86_64-only
    by Apple's licensing. event.c calls it unconditionally from the
    CLIENT_SURFACE_PRESENTED case, breaking the arm64-native winemac.drv.

Fix:
    Wrap the call site in event.c with the same `__x86_64__` guard.
    On arm64 host, D3DMetal is not loaded, so the event will never be
    posted — the case body becomes a comment.

---
 dlls/winemac.drv/event.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/event.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/event.c
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/event.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/event.c
@@ -400,7 +400,11 @@
         macdrv_app_quit_requested(event);
         break;
     case CLIENT_SURFACE_PRESENTED:    /* CW HACK 22435 */
+#if defined(__x86_64__)
 	macdrv_client_surface_presented(event);
+#else
+	/* MacRunner: D3DMetal-only event; not delivered on arm64 host. */
+#endif
 	break;
     case DISPLAYS_CHANGED:
         macdrv_displays_changed(event);
